 🚀 Getting Started

 Prerequisites

Make sure you have installed:

* Flutter SDK
* Dart SDK
* Android Studio or another Android development environment
* Visual Studio Code or Android Studio
* A Firebase project

 Installation

Clone the repository:


git clone https://github.com/MahnoorNaseer/secure_shed.git

Move into the project directory:


cd secure_shed


Install dependencies:

flutter pub get


Run the application:

flutter run


 Firebase Configuration

The application uses Firebase Authentication and Cloud Firestore.

For a new Firebase project, configure Firebase for the required Flutter platforms using FlutterFire CLI and generate the appropriate `firebase_options.dart` file.

> Do not commit private credentials, service-account files, or other sensitive Firebase configuration to a public repository.



